    "body": "## Change Summary\n\n- **What changed**: `LeRobotV2Dataset._decode_video_frames` now decodes all requested frames in a single container open via the existing batched backend API (`decode_video_frames_by_timestamps`), instead of one `av.open` + `seek` per frame (a list comprehension over `_decode_video_frame`).\n- **Which issue it addresses**: redundant per-frame container re-opening in the LeRobot v2.0/v2.1 dataset path. For FastWAM's LIBERO geometry (`num_video_frames=9`, `action_video_freq_ratio=4`, 2 cameras) that is 18 container opens per sample.\n- **Which modules are affected**: `loongforge/embodied/data/datasets/lerobot_dataset.py` only. Scope is `LeRobotV2Dataset`; `LeRobotV3Dataset` and `cosmos3/droid_lerobot_dataset.py` are unaffected (they already go through the upstream batched API).\n\n## Validation\n\n- [x] I ran the relevant local checks.\n- [ ] I added or updated tests where appropriate.\n- [x] I checked compatibility with existing APIs and configurations.\n\n**Bit-identity** (the critical check for a data-pipeline change):\n\n- `max|d| = 0` between the previous per-frame path and the new batched path: 48 samples x 8 episodes x 2 cameras = 528 arrays, overall sha256 equal, including episode-tail clamped duplicate frames.\n- Also `max|d| = 0` at frame level for both the `pyav` and `torchcodec` backends, 2 cameras x 3 episodes.\n\n**Performance** (8x A800-80GB):\n\n- Single-process microbenchmark (real LIBERO mp4, 9 frames): **147.8 -> 81.7 ms** per camera sample (**1.81x**).\n- End-to-end loader-only A/B (16 workers, batch 16, 60 batches; identical checkout with only the decode call toggled): **185.9 -> 204.7 samples/s (+10.1%)**.\n- Smoke: 5 training iterations on this branch (single LIBERO suite, `--lerobotdataset-version v2.1`) — finite loss / grad norm, 0 NaN.\n\n## CI, GPU, and Image Impact\n\n- [ ] This change affects dependencies, Dockerfiles, patches, or runtime environments.\n- [ ] GPU validation is required. Suggested suite: `llm_vlm` / `embodied`.\n- [x] No GPU or image validation is required.\n\n## Reviewer Notes\n\n- This does **not** speed up FastWAM training today: the data pipeline is not the bottleneck (batch-generator ~17.65 ms against a ~1507 ms step, ~1.2% waiting; pipeline capacity 175.5 samples/s vs 85.0 samples/s demand). The value is CPU/IO efficiency (9 fewer container opens per camera per sample, on every rank) and scaling headroom.\n- The batched `pyav` path decodes the whole `[min(ts), max(ts)]` window sequentially and selects by nearest timestamp, whereas `torchcodec` jumps to exact frames. That is a pre-existing, deliberate trade-off (see the `stream.thread_count = 1` note in `video_backends.py`), not introduced here.\n- `decode_video_frames_by_timestamps` was previously dead code on this path; this change wires it up.\n",
